# The Prettier gate is scoped to posts/ — the only directory whose bytes are
# published to the Jekyll Pages site (tooling/publish-to-pages.py copies each
# post body through byte-for-byte, so whatever ships here ships there).
#
# Everything else in this repo is authored to other conventions and is
# intentionally NOT formatted by this gate: social/ briefs and drafts, docs/
# prose, .claude/ specs, CLAUDE.md, test fixtures, tooling. Whole-repo
# formatting is a separate effort and is not implied by this file.
#
# This file is the SINGLE SOURCE of that scope: ignore everything, then unignore
# posts/. The npm scripts and CI run a bare `prettier .`, so this guard is what
# keeps them — and any ad-hoc `prettier .` a developer types — from reformatting
# unscoped files. (`/*` already covers node_modules/, so no separate entry.)
/*
!/posts/
